M.add(26639,"Add Service at another location copies the same work at this location's rates",S,L,P,
 preML,
 ["Read the row at this (non-home) location and its (i) note.","Use Add Service and read the modal's preview (no parts listed).","Check each added line's labour type and rate.","Confirm prices and parts are not copied, and tracking/completion stay organization-wide."],
 ["At a location other than the home location, the row reads exactly as at home (e.g. 'PM-A, Overdue · Aug 2026, 4 lines · 2.8 hours, Add Service') with an (i) explaining the lines were set up at the home location and the same work is added here at this location's rates.",
  "Add Service adds the same work (each canned line's name, description and hours) as new lines at this location's rates; prices and parts are not copied, because both are kept per location.",
  "Each copied line takes this location's labour type of the same name, or the default labour type where none matches, priced at that rate; a fixed-price line is priced the same way here.",
  "The Add Service modal's preview lists no parts here; tracking and completion stay organization-wide."],
 [("S16-R21","At a location other than the home location, the row reads exactly as it does at home, for example PM-A, Overdue · Aug 2026, 4 lines · 2.8 hours, Add Service, with an (i) beside it: PM-A's lines were set up at Calgary South. We add the same work here at Lethbridge's rates. Parts are not added; each line's note lists the parts Calgary South uses, for reference"),
  ("S16-N6","Add Service at a location other than the schedule's home location adds the same work, not the home location's lines: each canned line's name, description and hours, as new lines at this location's rates. Prices and parts are not copied, because both are kept per location. Tracking and completion stay organization-wide, per S18-R12"),
  ("S16-R22","Each copied line takes this location's labour type of the same name, or this location's default labour type where none matches, and is priced at that labour type's rate. A line that is fixed price at the home location is priced the same way here"),
  ("S16-R24","The Add Service modal is the standard one at every location. At a location other than the home location its preview lists no parts, because none are added; the card's (i) of S16-R21 is the only place that explains the copy")])
M.add(26639,"Each copied line carries an internal note listing the home location's parts",S,L,P,
 preML,
 ["After Add Service at a non-home location, open an added line.","Read its internal line note.","Open a fixed-price line's note."],
 ["Each copied line carries its own internal line note, headed 'Line note · Internal', not visible to the customer, reading 'Copied from Calgary South. Parts used there, for reference:' then each part's quantity, name and part number (e.g. '2 × Rotella T4 15W-40, 18.9L · RT4-189').",
  "A fixed-price line's note reads 'Copied from Calgary South. Fixed price there, priced at Lethbridge's rate here'."],
 [("S16-R23","Each copied line carries its own internal line note, headed Line note · Internal, not visible to the customer, reading Copied from Calgary South. Parts used there, for reference: and then each part's quantity, name and part number, for example 2 × Rotella T4 15W-40, 18.9L · RT4-189. A fixed-price line's note reads Copied from Calgary South. Fixed price there, priced at Lethbridge's rate here")])
M.add(26639,"Add Service toast + Undo; Remove until invoiced; neither deletes a line",S,L,P,
 pre,
 ["Use Add Service and read the toast ('PM-A added · 4 lines', with Undo).","Use Undo and confirm the row returns to Add Service and is no longer addressed.",
  "Add again, let the toast pass, then use Remove from the three-dot menu (before invoicing).","Confirm Undo/Remove do not delete the already-added lines (deleted by hand, per the line's own state)."],
 ["After Add Service a toast reads 'PM-A added · 4 lines' with Undo, for as long as the application's toasts stay.",
  "Once it is gone, the row's three-dot menu offers Remove (until the work order is invoiced); Undo and Remove both return the row to Add Service and it is no longer addressed, so the step after invoicing does not list it.",
  "Neither deletes a line: the lines already added stay on the work order and are deleted by hand; deleting the lines a service added does not unsatisfy that service."],
 [("S16-R25","After Add Service a toast reads PM-A added · 4 lines, with Undo, for as long as the application's toasts stay. Once it is gone, the row's three-dot menu offers Remove, for an Add Service made by mistake, until the work order is invoiced. Undo and Remove do the same: the row returns to Add Service and is no longer addressed on this work order, so the step after invoicing does not list it. Neither deletes a line. The lines already added stay on the work order, as any line does, and are deleted by hand, per S16-N4, because a line's own state decides whether it can be deleted"),
  ("S16-N4","Deleting the lines a service added does not unsatisfy that service. The advisor's statement governs, not which lines happen to remain")])
